 was over eight minutes behind the lead, and this decided the team event – Belgium winning the gold and Great Britain the silver medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Belgian champions, however, did not realize they had won a gold medal. They thought there was only an individual race in 1948, and simply got on the bus after the ride and were back in Belgium the next day. They were never given gold medals at the London Olympics. However, Van Roosbroeck later learned that they had won the team event and petitioned the IOC to have medals awarded to them. On 9 June 2010, Eugène Van Roosbroeck finally received his gold medal for this event, presented to him by " [:a {:href "/organizations/1"} "IOC"] " President " [:a {:href "/athletes/63485"} "Jacques Rogge"] ". His teammate Leon De Lathouwer was deceased and never received a gold medal, while Lode Wouters received a gold medal later in 2010 because he was too ill to attend the ceremony with Van Roosbroeck."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Belgium"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]] [:td {} "15-58:17.4"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/17211"} "Lode Wouters"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "5-18:16.2"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/14122"} "Leon De Lathouwer"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "5-18:16.2"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/17015"} "Eugène Van Roosbroeck"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "